   either:
     (a) retain them in full, or
     (b) prominently document, in the user interface and in any redistribution,
         how they were changed or weakened, and why.
   Distributing a version that silently removes, disables, or relabels these
   safeguards is prohibited.

3. NO CLINICAL OR OPERATIONAL USE. The Software is a research prototype. It
   MUST NOT be used:
     * as a clinical diagnostic device;
     * as an operational public-health, public-safety, or biosecurity system;
     * to trigger automated public-health interventions;
     * to communicate surveillance findings to the public as fact.

4. NO MISREPRESENTATION. The Software contains no trained machine-learning
   model, no validated performance metric, and no real surveillance data.
   You may not market, deploy, or describe a derivative work in a way that
   implies validated operational capability without independent peer-reviewed
   evidence.

5. SYNTHETIC DATA LABELING. All deterministic synthetic outputs must remain
   visibly labelled "SIMULATED" (or an equivalent honest disclosure) at the
   point of display.

